cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite the accompanying paper and this repository."
title: "Extending pyGMT into Deep Time via GPlately"
abstract: >-
  An open, reproducible tutorial suite of eighty Jupyter notebooks that couples
  GPlately plate-tectonic reconstructions with pyGMT publication-quality maps,
  charts, and scientific plots. The suite is organised into eleven thematic
  clusters -- foundational paleo-Earth cartography; plate kinematics and
  tectonics; plate-model quality-control diagnostics; zircon-based tectonic-
  setting analyses; mantle dynamics and dynamic topography; paleomagnetism;
  paleo-geography, paleo-topography and thermochronology; sedimentary-basin
  architecture; paleo-biogeography; paleoclimate; and reconstruction-driven
  exploration for Earth resources -- and progresses within each cluster from an
  introductory single-concept example to a research-grade workflow. The suite
  executes on a laptop, ships with executed outputs preserved for instant visual
  feedback on GitHub, and is accompanied by per-notebook learning objectives,
  references, and an "Extend this" section. Nine of the eighty notebooks
  additionally depend on a large companion data archive distributed separately
  via Zenodo.
type: software
